R_GE_7 r=12: r does not divide k -> t=1/12 has clearance >=1/12; r divides k -> w>=14r=168>T=132
DILATED_DECK: D=c/gcd(c,w)>=2 -> circular_span=1-1/D>=1/2>2/13; therefore full closed-danger incidence forces D=1 and c|w
GERM_CLOSURE: the surviving complementary owner is -1/13 at every lifted splice; a left half-germ is core-safe, and closedness of {||wt||<=1/13} carries danger to the splice
DESCENT: 13 does not divide c and w congruent cr (mod 13), together with c|w, give w/c=r+13k; k=0 restores the AP and k>=1 is the loose W_k(r) branch

